<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Prague bourse raises main mkt turnover requirement.</title>
<headline>Prague bourse raises main mkt turnover requirement.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Prague Stock Exchange (PSE) said on Tuesday that its listing committee had agreed to raise the average daily turnover which an issue must maintain to be listed on the main market to one million crowns from the current 300,000 crowns.</p>
<p>The new turnover requirement, which would be averaged over the previous 12-months, would begin from January 1, 1998, PSE spokesman Milan Vodicka said in a statement.</p>
</text>
